<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamim ibn Buluggin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamim ibn Buluggin was a Zirid prince who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Málaga from about 1073 to 1090, while his brother Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. The brothers quarrelled over territory, and both were deposed by the Almoravid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a> in 1090 and sent into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, ending Zirid rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p></div>
